{"nodes": [{"id": "constitution", "label": "loom \u2014 Constitution", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CONSTITUTION.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "constitution_the_entities", "label": "The entities", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CONSTITUTION.md", "source_location": "CONSTITUTION.md#the-entities", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "| Entity | Where it lives | |---|---| | [Skill](CONTEXT.md#skill) | `SKILLS/<bucket>/<slug>/SKILL.md` | | [Workflow](CONTEXT.md#workflow) | `workflows/<name>/` | | [Agent](CONTEXT.md#agent) | `agents/<name>.md` | | [Adapter](CONTEXT.md#adapter) | `adapters/<harness>/` | | [Harness](CONTEXT.md#harness) | external \u2014 not ours, we target it | | [Setup contract](CONTEXT.md#setup-contract) | `contract/` | | [Wiki](CONTEXT.md#wiki) | `wiki/` | | [Wrapper](CONTEXT.md#wrapper) | `commands/` | | Distribut"}, {"id": "constitution_how_they_compose", "label": "How they compose", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CONSTITUTION.md", "source_location": "CONSTITUTION.md#how-they-compose", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The spine runs one way, and it is worth stating plainly because the two ends are easy to confuse:"}, {"id": "constitution_the_binding_rules", "label": "The binding rules", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CONSTITUTION.md", "source_location": "CONSTITUTION.md#the-binding-rules", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "1. **Prose first.** Structured output \u2014 YAML, JSON, tool config \u2014 lives solely in the adapter    layer. A workflow or skill expresses policy; the adapter's interpreting agent maps it onto    the target environment's real capabilities. See    [workflows/index.md](workflows/index.md#prose-first-principle)."}, {"id": "constitution_quality", "label": "Quality", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CONSTITUTION.md", "source_location": "CONSTITUTION.md#quality", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "`scripts/quality.sh` **is** loom's [quality baseline](CONTEXT.md#quality-baseline) \u2014 the floors for `scripts/loom/`, and the commands that prove them. Per [quality-baseline](wiki/patterns/quality-baseline.md) ([ADR-017](wiki/adr/adr-017-quality-baseline.md)) a project's floor belongs in its own committed tooling, with loom holding only a pointer; the script carries the floors and the reasons its command shapes cannot be simplified."}, {"id": "constitution_the_gate", "label": "The gate", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CONSTITUTION.md", "source_location": "CONSTITUTION.md#the-gate", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "`scripts/validate.sh` is the mechanical enforcement of this constitution: frontmatter, link resolution, anchor existence, orphan reachability, and registry consistency."}, {"id": "constitution_amendment", "label": "Amendment", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CONSTITUTION.md", "source_location": "CONSTITUTION.md#amendment", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "This document changes by [ADR](CONTEXT.md#adr-architecture-decision-record). A rule here that a decision supersedes is rewritten, not annotated, and the ADR is linked from the rule it changed."}], "edges": [{"source": "constitution", "target": "vision", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CONSTITUTION.md", "source_location": "CONSTITUTION.md", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "constitution", "target": "context", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CONSTITUTION.md", "source_location": "CONSTITUTION.md", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "constitution